-- title:
--   Galois twists of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise application of $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}$ times the rational $j$-numerator power series. Assume $\Gamma = \mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ acts on $A$ by ring automorphisms with $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{A,L}(s \cdot a) = s(\mathrm{algebraMap}_{A,L}(a))$. Write $X$ for the two-chart model over $A$: the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, with structure morphism $\mathrm{modelTo}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and chart immersions $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$. Then there are families $s \mapsto w_s \in \mathrm{End}(X)$, $s \mapsto \rho_s$ and $s \mapsto \rho'_s$ of ring automorphisms of the two chart algebras, indexed by $\Gamma$, such that: $w_s$ followed by $\mathrm{modelTo}$ equals $\mathrm{modelTo}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the automorphism of $A$ given by $s$; $w_1 = \mathrm{id}$ and $w_{ss'}$ equals $w_s$ followed by $w_{s'}$; for $b$ in either chart algebra the image of $\rho_s b$ (respectively $\rho'_s b$) in $L((q))$ is obtained from that of $b$ by applying $s$ to all coefficients; $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ followed by $w_s$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_s)$ followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, and likewise for $\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and $\rho'_s$; and the preimage under $w_s$ of the open range of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ is that open range.
--
--   This provides the descent datum, or Galois twisting action, of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ on the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the discrete valuation ring $A$: an action by model morphisms covering the action on the base, semilinear over it and compatible with both chart presentations. It is used downstream in the analysis of the special fibre of this model and of its Jacobian, in particular in the comparison of sections and of diamond operators with the Galois action.
